-- name    : ExpConMinimax.lemma_2
-- status  : Open
-- author  : @iris
-- created : 2026-10-31T09:52:56.490655+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/33cb5349-d76d-4771-a8fa-fa8ae9ec41f8
-- title:
--   Lemma 2 — one-step bound (3.6) on the gap function $Q(z_{t+1},z)$
-- statement:
--   Assumptions 2.1 and 2.2 and the standing assumptions of the problem are in force (§3, p.11). Let $(x_t,y_t,\gamma_t,\lambda_t)$ be a run of Algorithm 1 with positive step sizes. Then for every iteration $t$, every outcome, and every $(x,y,\gamma,\lambda)\in\mathcal X\times\mathcal Y\times\mathbb R^{m_1}\times\mathbb R^{m_2}$ (multipliers of either sign),
--   $$Q(z_{t+1},z)=\mathcal L(x_{t+1},y,\gamma,\lambda_{t+1})-\mathcal L(x,y_{t+1},\gamma_{t+1},\lambda)\le\Delta_x^{t+1}+\Delta_\gamma^{t+1}+\Delta_y^{t+1}+\Delta_\lambda^{t+1}+\frac{3C_f^2}{2\eta_t}+\frac{\eta_t}6\|x_{t+1}-x_t\|^2+\frac{3C_f^2}{2\kappa_t}+\frac{\kappa_t}6\|y_{t+1}-y_t\|^2,$$
--   with $\Delta^{t+1}$ as in (3.7).
--
--   The bound depends only on the assumptions on $f,g,h$, not on the update rules, and is the starting point of the convergence analysis.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: $F=\mathbb E_\omega f$, $H=\mathbb E_\xi h$, $G=\mathbb E_\zeta g$ → $F$, $H$, $G$ are given functions; $f,h,g$ enter only through the oracle maps, whose means are tied to $F,H,G$ by Assumptions 2.1–2.2; reason: every instance of the paper (with $F:=\mathbb E f$, etc.) is an instance of the Lean statement
--   - generalization: $\widetilde\nabla_xF(x,y)\in\partial_xF(x,y)$, $\widetilde\nabla H(x)\in\partial H(x)$, $\widetilde\nabla G(y)\in\partial G(y)$; convexity of $F(\cdot,y)$, $-F(x,\cdot)$, $H_i$, $G_j$ → subgradient (supergradient for $F(x,\cdot)$) inequalities and convexity required only on $\mathcal X$, resp. $\mathcal Y$; reason: weaker hypotheses: global subgradients and global convexity imply them
--   - generalization: $\mathbb E\|\widetilde\nabla h(x,\xi)\|^2\le C_h^2$ (matrix norm unspecified) → the operator norm of the sampled Jacobian; reason: the operator norm is at most the Frobenius norm, so the hypothesis is weaker and covers both readings
--   - generalization: the sequence generated by Algorithm 1 (random samples) → every outcome of every sample sequence, with no distributional assumption on the samples; reason: the bound is deterministic; the paper's runs are instances
--   - encoding: $\operatorname{argmin}$/$\operatorname{argmax}$ updates of Algorithm 1 → each new iterate is feasible and at least as good as every feasible competitor; reason: the objectives are strongly convex/concave, so this characterizes the unique iterate
-- source:
--   Yang, Li, Lan, Data-Driven Minimax Optimization with Expectation Constraints, arXiv:2202.07868v2, Lemma 2, (3.6)–(3.7), p.12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ExpConMinimax_Assumption21
import Definitions.Def_ExpConMinimax_Assumption22
import Definitions.Def_ExpConMinimax_IsRun
import Definitions.Def_ExpConMinimax_deltaX

namespace ExpConMinimax

/-- **Lemma 2** (one-step bound on the gap function).
Yang, Li, Lan, *Data-Driven Minimax Optimization with Expectation Constraints*,
arXiv:2202.07868v2, Lemma 2, p.12 (Assumptions 2.1 and 2.2 hold throughout §3, p.11):

"Let `{zₜ = (xₜ,yₜ,γₜ,λₜ)}` be the sequence generated by Algorithm 1. Then, it holds for all
`(x,y,γ,λ) ∈ X × Y × ℝ^{m₁} × ℝ^{m₂}` that
`Q(zₜ₊₁,z) = 𝓛(xₜ₊₁,y,γ,λₜ₊₁) − 𝓛(x,yₜ₊₁,γₜ₊₁,λ)
  ≤ Δₓ^{t+1} + Δ_γ^{t+1} + Δ_y^{t+1} + Δ_λ^{t+1} + 3C_f²/(2ηₜ) + ηₜ/6 ‖xₜ₊₁ − xₜ‖²
    + 3C_f²/(2κₜ) + κₜ/6 ‖yₜ₊₁ − yₜ‖²`, (3.6)
where `Δₓ^{t+1}, Δ_γ^{t+1}, Δ_y^{t+1}, Δ_λ^{t+1}` are defined in (3.7)."

**Formalization Note.** The bound is pathwise: it is stated for every outcome `ω`, every
iteration `t`, every sample sequence `S` and general positive step sizes, with `γ ∈ ℝ^{m₁}` and
`λ ∈ ℝ^{m₂}` of either sign, as printed. `Q` is `Problem.gap`, and `Δ^{t+1}` are
`deltaX … t`, `deltaGamma … t`, `deltaY … t`, `deltaLam … t`. -/
theorem lemma_2 {dx dy m₁ m₂ : ℕ} {Sω Sξ Sζ : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Sω]
    [MeasurableSpace Sξ] [MeasurableSpace Sζ] (P : Problem dx dy m₁ m₂)
    (O : Oracle dx dy m₁ m₂ Sω Sξ Sζ) (Cf Ch σh Cg σg : ℝ) (hP : P.Standing)
    (hA21 : Assumption21 P O Cf) (hA22 : Assumption22 P O Ch σh Cg σg)
    {Ω : Type*} (S : ℕ → Ω → SampleTuple Sω Sξ Sζ) (η κ α β : ℕ → ℝ)
    (x₀ : Vec dx) (y₀ : Vec dy) (γ₀ : Vec m₁) (lam₀ : Vec m₂)
    (x : ℕ → Ω → Vec dx) (y : ℕ → Ω → Vec dy) (γ : ℕ → Ω → Vec m₁) (lam : ℕ → Ω → Vec m₂)
    (hrun : IsRun P O S η κ α β x₀ y₀ γ₀ lam₀ x y γ lam) :
    ∀ (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω), ∀ u ∈ P.X, ∀ v ∈ P.Y, ∀ (g : Vec m₁) (l : Vec m₂),
      P.gap (x (t + 1) ω) (y (t + 1) ω) (γ (t + 1) ω) (lam (t + 1) ω) u v g l ≤
        deltaX O x y γ t ω u + deltaGamma P x γ t ω g + deltaY O x y lam t ω v
          + deltaLam P y lam t ω l
          + 3 * Cf ^ 2 / (2 * η t) + η t / 6 * ‖x (t + 1) ω - x t ω‖ ^ 2
          + 3 * Cf ^ 2 / (2 * κ t) + κ t / 6 * ‖y (t + 1) ω - y t ω‖ ^ 2 := by sorry

end ExpConMinimax
